<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Puebla-Tlaxcala Valley</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Puebla-Tlaxcala Valley is a highland basin of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, east of the volcanoes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/popocatepetl">Popocatépetl</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iztaccihuatl">Iztaccíhuatl</a>, shared by the modern states of Puebla and Tlaxcala. It was home to major centres such as Cholula, Cacaxtla, Tlaxcala and Huexotzinco. After the Spanish conquest the city of Puebla was founded there in 1531.</p></div>
